{"id": "EUVD-2026-38986", "enisaUuid": "9244fc9e-ad89-3217-8e41-34a69a0a7eed", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvdpa: use generic driver_override infrastructure\n\nWhen a driver is probed through __driver_attach(), the bus' match()\ncallback is called without the device lock held, thus accessing the\ndriver_override field without a lock, which can cause a UAF.\n\nFix this by using the driver-core driver_override infrastructure taking\ncare of proper locking internally.\n\nNote that calling match() from __driver_attach() without the device lock\nheld is intentional. [1]", "datePublished": "2026-06-24T16:30:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:42:06", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4005cb89139f7c9af85046b241dcf3fa2e1b3559", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4eab1a74a498f0bf19f102f9362e9deef9307aea", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/654ef9c33e138ede6734ac286282df9faf83cd11", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fb5cb4913ce333cc4647722e8c2b8378e12f2464", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/85bb534ff12aab6916058897b39c748940a7a4c6"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jmxg-xc7h-vhvv", "CVE-2026-53118"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0a198cbe-78a3-39af-a2f3-b938921d0867", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "539fec78edb4e084e7c532affc56cc42d4ceea4b <85bb534ff12aab6916058897b39c748940a7a4c6"}, {"id": "0b7f2ffe-9725-3fbe-8508-ec4c6b61b35c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "39ace23b-088d-3823-817e-675e2cff4c63", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "539fec78edb4e084e7c532affc56cc42d4ceea4b <4eab1a74a498f0bf19f102f9362e9deef9307aea"}, {"id": "502ee8d0-ad0a-3d94-a60e-22d7f3431305", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "7fd106cf-05c2-3176-bd45-1ba934bf5d3f", "product": {"na